      Open south and east windows for a natural cross-breeze that freshens the air and warms the house for free.
      
      Close up by 12:00 PM before outdoor air warms past indoor. If the house dips below 70°F tonight, the heater comes back on automatically.
      
      If you head out, not much changes today — after about 15 minutes I'll widen the band to 60–80°F to save energy, and restore comfort when you're back.
      
      If you want to open a window for some fresh air, go for it — the thermostat is holding 70–75°F today. Enjoy the breeze. If the heat or AC does need to run while a window is still open, I'll give it 10 minutes and then pause until you close up.
      
      📋 Today's Steps
      ----------------------------------------
        • 6:30 AM: CA switches to the daytime comfort band, 70°F to 75°F.
